WEBVTT

00:00:05.425 --> 00:00:08.025
YESSS: Yo, Ralph,
you in here, dude?

00:00:08.185 --> 00:00:09.785
Hey, I got to show you...

00:00:11.065 --> 00:00:12.305
Oh.

00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:14.945
First rule of the Internet...

00:00:15.105 --> 00:00:17.665
do not read the comments.

00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:19.425
I should have told you that.

00:00:20.345 --> 00:00:21.385
Look.

00:00:21.585 --> 00:00:24.425
This place can bring out
the worst in some people...

00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:26.225
but you gotta ignore all this.

00:00:26.385 --> 00:00:29.425
This isn't about you, Ralph.
It's about them.

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:31.745
I don't care. It's fine.

00:00:31.825 --> 00:00:33.105
(SNIFFLES)

00:00:33.185 --> 00:00:36.505
People hated me my whole life
for being the bad guy.

00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:38.745
It's just a good reminder

00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:41.425
that this is the only heart
that really matters.

00:00:42.065 --> 00:00:43.465
Vanellope gave me this...

00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:45.105
and as long as she likes me...

00:00:45.265 --> 00:00:46.905
I don't need anybody else.

00:00:47.105 --> 00:00:48.585
And I sure
don't need the Internet.

00:00:48.745 --> 00:00:50.065
Hold on. (CHUCKLES)

00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:52.105
It's not all bad.

00:00:52.265 --> 00:00:53.905
The Internet
can also be a place...

00:00:54.065 --> 00:00:56.385
where you find a steering
wheel at one website...

00:00:56.545 --> 00:00:59.745
and make enough money
to buy it at another one.

00:00:59.905 --> 00:01:02.065
Congratulations, Ralph.
You did it.

00:01:02.225 --> 00:01:03.345
Wait, really?

00:01:03.505 --> 00:01:05.505
Yes, check your
Buzzzy account.

00:01:05.705 --> 00:01:08.705
You needed 27K,
you got over 30 grand!

00:01:08.865 --> 00:01:09.905
Oh, my gosh!

00:01:10.065 --> 00:01:11.145
This is great!

00:01:11.305 --> 00:01:13.265
Thank you, Yesss. I couldn't
have done it without you!

00:01:13.465 --> 00:01:14.705
That's really true.

00:01:14.865 --> 00:01:16.105
Hey, eboy?

00:01:16.305 --> 00:01:17.505
What do you need, ace?

00:01:17.665 --> 00:01:19.265
Can you give me a ride?

00:01:19.425 --> 00:01:21.705
Let's hop along, Cassidy.

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:25.425
Come on, song, come on.

00:01:26.225 --> 00:01:27.785
I'm reflecting.

00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:29.625
What is it that I want?

00:01:29.785 --> 00:01:30.785
What is my quest?

00:01:30.945 --> 00:01:33.345
(IN SING-SONG VOICE)
What is my dream?

00:01:34.305 --> 00:01:35.305
(GROANS)

00:01:35.385 --> 00:01:37.425
Well, ladies, I tried.

00:01:37.585 --> 00:01:40.185
No song for this princess,
I guess.

00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:42.225
-(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)
-Ooh! Huh.

00:01:43.665 --> 00:01:45.385
How does this thing work?

00:01:45.585 --> 00:01:47.065
-(GASPS)
-Hey, kid, can you see me?

00:01:47.225 --> 00:01:48.945
Yeah!
Yeah, you're right there.

00:01:49.105 --> 00:01:51.065
We did it! We got the money!

00:01:51.225 --> 00:01:53.425
No way, Ralph! That's great!

00:01:53.585 --> 00:01:55.905
I'm on my way to ebay
right now with the eboy.

00:01:56.065 --> 00:01:57.145
We're almost there, champ.

00:01:57.345 --> 00:01:58.345
Good work, eboy.

00:01:58.425 --> 00:02:00.545
Hey, meet me out in front of
ebay in five minutes, okay?

00:02:00.705 --> 00:02:02.305
Okay, I'll see you soon.

00:02:02.465 --> 00:02:03.945
We're going home, kid!

00:02:04.145 --> 00:02:06.425
Our lives can finally
get back to normal.

00:02:06.505 --> 00:02:07.665
Whoo-hoo!

00:02:09.705 --> 00:02:12.945
Wow, I can't believe it.
I get to go home.

00:02:13.105 --> 00:02:14.225
So, I guess that's it.

00:02:14.305 --> 00:02:17.745
I guess I just wanted a...
a steering wheel.

00:02:18.465 --> 00:02:20.585
And now, I got it, so...

00:02:20.945 --> 00:02:22.425
whoo-hoo. (SIGHS)

00:02:25.585 --> 00:02:26.665
(GASPS)

00:02:27.265 --> 00:02:28.385
Slaughter Race?

00:02:28.465 --> 00:02:30.185
(HELICOPTER HOVERING)

00:02:35.865 --> 00:02:39.825
(SINGING) What can it be that
calls me to this place today?

00:02:39.985 --> 00:02:42.545
This lawless car ballet?

00:02:42.705 --> 00:02:45.185
What can it be?

00:02:46.225 --> 00:02:50.345
Am I a baby pigeon
sprouting wings to soar?

00:02:50.505 --> 00:02:52.105
Was that a metaphor?

00:02:52.265 --> 00:02:55.385
Hey, there's a dollar store

00:02:55.465 --> 00:02:58.705
Look!
I'm rhyming

00:02:58.905 --> 00:03:03.025
My spirits climbing

00:03:03.185 --> 00:03:07.105
As I'm called through
this fog of mace

00:03:08.105 --> 00:03:11.425
To this place called

00:03:11.625 --> 00:03:15.505
Slaughter Race

00:03:17.025 --> 00:03:18.305
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:03:18.425 --> 00:03:19.905
Welcome back
Watch your head

00:03:20.065 --> 00:03:21.825
Hate to see you end up dead

00:03:21.985 --> 00:03:23.545
Let's get this party rollin'

00:03:23.705 --> 00:03:25.305
Is that appliance stolen?

00:03:25.465 --> 00:03:26.585
-We have
-Fallen wires

00:03:26.745 --> 00:03:27.945
-Dumpster fires
-Creepy clowns

00:03:28.145 --> 00:03:29.265
And burning tires

00:03:29.425 --> 00:03:30.825
That great white in the sewer

00:03:30.905 --> 00:03:32.265
You'll be happy
that you knew her

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.345
Fin bump!

00:03:33.425 --> 00:03:34.785
Dogs and cats
They sure taste great

00:03:34.945 --> 00:03:36.705
With a side of license plate

00:03:36.865 --> 00:03:38.265
Some find us deplorable

00:03:38.425 --> 00:03:40.265
Well, I think you're adorable

00:03:40.425 --> 00:03:43.745
We may be a motley crew
But our hearts ring true

00:03:43.945 --> 00:03:46.745
And just for you
A face tattoo

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:50.145
(INSTRUMENTAL JAZZ
MUSIC PLAYING)

00:04:02.625 --> 00:04:06.345
CHORUS: Slaughter Race

00:04:08.145 --> 00:04:11.665
My heart's in flight
And wow, it's a blast

00:04:11.825 --> 00:04:14.825
Feels like my dreams
are real at last

00:04:15.025 --> 00:04:18.985
No trace of a frown
upon your face

00:04:19.145 --> 00:04:22.425
VANELLOPE: Flying so fast
SHANK: Setting the pace

00:04:22.585 --> 00:04:26.185
-Living the life
-Loving the chase

00:04:26.345 --> 00:04:29.345
-Now is the time
-Here is the place

00:04:29.505 --> 00:04:33.665
This Slaughter Race!

00:04:43.745 --> 00:04:47.105
I know I should go

00:04:47.305 --> 00:04:51.025
But home feels so slow

00:04:51.225 --> 00:04:57.185
These roads are paved
with dreams

00:04:57.345 --> 00:04:59.985
(ECHOING) Happy dreams
Not creepy clown dreams

00:05:01.465 --> 00:05:04.345
What would Ralph say

00:05:04.865 --> 00:05:08.825
If it turns out I stay?

00:05:08.985 --> 00:05:12.825
In this place called

00:05:12.985 --> 00:05:18.305
Slaughter

00:05:18.465 --> 00:05:23.545
Race

00:05:29.185 --> 00:05:33.105
In this place called

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:36.945
Slaughter

00:05:37.985 --> 00:05:42.025
Race

